Current flow is direct and localized:

`spawn_pi` schema (`src/tools.ts`) → `SpawnTask.placement` validation (`src/domain.ts`) → `task.placement ?? "tab
"` (`src/batch.ts`) → `StartChildRequest.placement` (`src/herdr/host.ts`) → Herdr `tab.create` or `pane.split`.

The extension already loads strict JSON from `~/.pi/agent/herdr-subagents.json` in `s
rc/model-routing.ts`; unknown keys are rejected and missing config receives defaults. That is the narrowest place to own placement.

## Draft recommendation

Add `"placement"` under `"defaults"`:\
n
```json
{
  "orchestrator": { "enabled": false },
  "defaults": {
    "placement": "tab",
    "model": ["openai-codex/gpt-5.6-luna"],
    "thinking": "medium"
  }
}
```

Why `defaults.pl
acement`:
- It is a global child-launch default alongside model/thinking.
- It avoids adding another top-level section for one enum.
- Role documents remain unable to control placement.
- Missing 
config and missing `defaults.placement` both behave as `"tab"`.

